-- ====== NEET — BIOLOGY (90 questions) ======
('NEET','Biology','Cell Biology','easy','The powerhouse of the cell is:','["Mitochondria","Nucleus","Ribosome","Golgi apparatus"]',0,'Mitochondria produce ATP through cellular respiration — hence called the powerhouse of the cell.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Cell Biology','medium','Which organelle is responsible for protein synthesis?','["Ribosome","Mitochondria","Lysosome","Centrosome"]',0,'Ribosomes are the sites of protein synthesis (translation).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Cell Biology','hard','In which phase of cell cycle does DNA replication occur?','["S phase","G1 phase","G2 phase","M phase"]',0,'DNA replication occurs during the S (Synthesis) phase of interphase.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Cell Division','medium','Crossing over occurs during which stage of meiosis?','["Pachytene of Prophase I","Metaphase I","Anaphase II","Zygotene of Prophase I"]',0,'Crossing over (exchange of segments between non-sister chromatids) occurs at pachytene stage.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Cell Division','hard','At the end of meiosis II, how many haploid cells are formed from one diploid cell?','["4","2","8","1"]',0,'Meiosis I produces 2 cells; meiosis II produces 4 haploid cells total.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','easy','Mendel`s law of segregation states that:','["Alleles separate during gamete formation","Genes are linked on chromosomes","Dominant alleles mask recessive","Genes assort independently"]',0,'Law of Segregation: two alleles for each trait separate during gamete formation.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','medium','In ABO blood group, a person with genotype I^A I^B has blood group:','["AB","A","B","O"]',0,'I^A and I^B are codominant — both A and B antigens are expressed → blood group AB.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','hard','A colourblind father and normal (homozygous) mother have children. What fraction of sons are colourblind?','["0","1/2","1","1/4"]',0,'Mother is X^N X^N, father is X^c Y. Sons receive X^N from mother → all sons are normal (0 colourblind).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Molecular Biology','medium','Which enzyme unwinds the DNA double helix during replication?','["Helicase","DNA Polymerase","Ligase","Primase"]',0,'Helicase breaks hydrogen bonds between base pairs to unwind the double helix.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Molecular Biology','hard','The anticodon on tRNA that pairs with codon AUG (start) is:','["UAC","UAG","AUG","TAC"]',0,'Anticodon is complementary and antiparallel: AUG → UAC (reading 3→5 on tRNA = 5-UAC-3).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Evolution','easy','The theory of natural selection was proposed by:','["Charles Darwin","Jean-Baptiste Lamarck","Hugo de Vries","Gregor Mendel"]',0,'Charles Darwin proposed the theory of natural selection in "On the Origin of Species" (1859).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Evolution','medium','Which is the correct sequence of origin of life?','["Chemical evolution → Protobionts → Eukaryotes → Prokaryotes","Chemical evolution → Protobionts → Prokaryotes → Eukaryotes","Prokaryotes → Eukaryotes → Chemical evolution","Protobionts → Chemical evolution → Prokaryotes"]',1,'Life: Chemical evolution → Protobionts (coacervates) → Prokaryotes → Eukaryotes.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','easy','The normal range of blood pressure (systolic/diastolic) is:','["120/80 mmHg","180/120 mmHg","80/60 mmHg","140/90 mmHg"]',0,'Normal blood pressure is 120 mmHg systolic and 80 mmHg diastolic.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','medium','Glucagon is secreted by which cells of the pancreas?','["Alpha cells","Beta cells","Delta cells","Acinar cells"]',0,'Glucagon (raises blood glucose) is secreted by α (alpha) cells of islets of Langerhans.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','hard','Which part of the nephron is impermeable to water but permeable to electrolytes?','["Ascending limb of loop of Henle","Descending limb","Proximal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct"]',0,'The ascending thick limb of loop of Henle is impermeable to water but actively transports Na⁺/Cl⁻.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Physiology','medium','C4 plants have a special anatomy called:','["Kranz anatomy","Mesophyll anatomy","Bundle sheath only","Guard cell anatomy"]',0,'C4 plants have Kranz anatomy: mesophyll cells surrounding bundle sheath cells rich in chloroplasts.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Physiology','hard','The Q10 (temperature coefficient) for biological reactions is approximately:','["2","1","10","5"]',0,'Q10 ≈ 2, meaning biological reaction rates approximately double for every 10°C rise in temperature.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','medium','The relationship between mycorrhizae and plant roots is an example of:','["Mutualism","Parasitism","Commensalism","Amensalism"]',0,'Mycorrhizae (fungi) and plant roots: fungi get carbohydrates, plants get minerals — mutualism.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','hard','In a lake ecosystem, if energy available at producer level is 10⁶ kJ, energy at secondary consumer level (10% law) is:','["10,000 kJ","1000 kJ","100 kJ","100,000 kJ"]',0,'10% law: producer → 10⁵ kJ (primary) → 10⁴ kJ (secondary consumer).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Reproduction','medium','Double fertilization in angiosperms results in:','["Seed and endosperm","Fruit and seed","Two zygotes","Endosperm only"]',0,'Double fertilization: one sperm + egg → zygote; one sperm + polar nuclei → endosperm (3n).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Reproduction','hard','Which hormone maintains corpus luteum during early pregnancy?','["hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin)","LH","FSH","Progesterone"]',0,'hCG secreted by trophoblast maintains corpus luteum in early pregnancy, sustaining progesterone secretion.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Biotechnology','medium','Restriction endonucleases cut DNA at specific sequences called:','["Palindromic sequences","Promoter sequences","Operator sequences","Introns"]',0,'Restriction enzymes recognize and cut at palindromic sequences (read the same on both strands 5→3).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Biotechnology','hard','Recombinant DNA technology was first demonstrated using:','["EcoRI restriction enzyme","Sanger sequencing","PCR","Southern blotting"]',0,'EcoRI was the first restriction enzyme used to demonstrate recombinant DNA technology in 1970s.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Kingdom','easy','Which division of plants does not have vascular tissue?','["Bryophyta","Pteridophyta","Gymnospermae","Angiospermae"]',0,'Bryophytes (mosses, liverworts) lack true vascular tissue (xylem and phloem).','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Kingdom','medium','Gametophyte generation is dominant in:','["Bryophytes","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms"]',0,'In bryophytes, the gametophyte (haploid) generation is dominant and photosynthetic.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Animal Kingdom','easy','Bilateral symmetry and triploblastic body plan first appeared in:','["Platyhelminthes","Porifera","Cnidaria","Echinodermata"]',0,'Platyhelminthes (flatworms) are the first bilaterally symmetrical triploblastic animals.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Animal Kingdom','medium','Which class of Mollusca includes the largest number of species?','["Gastropoda","Bivalvia","Cephalopoda","Scaphopoda"]',0,'Gastropoda (snails, slugs) is the largest class of Mollusca.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Structural Organisation','easy','Goblet cells secrete:','["Mucus","Enzymes","Hormones","Bile"]',0,'Goblet cells are unicellular glands in epithelium that secrete mucus for lubrication and protection.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','medium','The correct sequence of impulse conduction in heart:','["SA node → AV node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibres","AV node → SA node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibres","SA node → Bundle of His → AV node → Purkinje fibres","Purkinje fibres → SA node → AV node"]',0,'SA node (pacemaker) → AV node → Bundle of His → Purkinje fibres → ventricular walls.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','hard','Which enzyme converts fibrinogen to fibrin during blood clotting?','["Thrombin","Prothrombin","Thromboplastin","Plasmin"]',0,'Thrombin (from prothrombin) converts fibrinogen (soluble) to fibrin (insoluble) to form a clot.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','medium','Lichens are symbiotic associations of:','["Fungi and algae","Fungi and bacteria","Algae and bacteria","Mosses and fungi"]',0,'Lichens are mutualistic symbiosis between fungi (mycobiont) and algae or cyanobacteria (photobiont).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','medium','Which type of mutation involves addition or deletion of a base pair?','["Frameshift mutation","Missense mutation","Nonsense mutation","Silent mutation"]',0,'Insertion or deletion of one or more nucleotides shifts the reading frame — frameshift mutation.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Molecular Biology','medium','The enzyme that adds RNA primer during DNA replication is:','["Primase","Helicase","DNA Polymerase I","Ligase"]',0,'Primase synthesizes short RNA primers to provide 3-OH end for DNA polymerase to start synthesis.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Photosynthesis','easy','The site of dark reactions of photosynthesis is:','["Stroma of chloroplast","Thylakoid membrane","Grana","Cytoplasm"]',0,'Calvin cycle (dark reactions) occurs in the stroma of the chloroplast.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Photosynthesis','hard','Z-scheme in light reactions involves:','["PS I and PS II working in series","Only PS I","Only PS II","PS I and PS II in parallel"]',0,'Z-scheme: PS II → electron transport chain → PS I → NADPH; both photosystems work in series.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Respiration','medium','Net ATP produced per molecule of glucose in aerobic respiration:','["36-38","2","10","18"]',0,'Aerobic respiration yields approximately 36-38 ATP per glucose molecule.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Respiration','hard','The enzyme that catalyses the conversion of pyruvate to Acetyl CoA is:','["Pyruvate dehydrogenase","Pyruvate kinase","Phosphofructokinase","Citrate synthase"]',0,'Pyruvate dehydrogenase complex converts pyruvate → Acetyl CoA + CO₂ + NADH in the mitochondrial matrix.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Growth','medium','Which plant hormone promotes fruit ripening?','["Ethylene","Gibberellin","Auxin","Cytokinin"]',0,'Ethylene (a gas) promotes fruit ripening, leaf abscission, and senescence.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Growth','hard','Vernalization refers to:','["Cold treatment to promote flowering","Day-length effect on flowering","Auxin-induced cell elongation","Gibberellin-induced stem elongation"]',0,'Vernalization is the cold treatment that promotes flowering in plants requiring cold to flower (e.g., wheat).','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Immunology','medium','Which type of immunity involves antibodies?','["Humoral immunity","Cell-mediated immunity","Innate immunity","Passive immunity only"]',0,'Humoral immunity involves B lymphocytes producing antibodies against antigens.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Immunology','hard','The full form of ELISA is:','["Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Enzyme-Linked Immunosuppression Assay","Electrolytic Ligase Immunosorbent Assay","Enzyme-Linked Isolation Standard Assay"]',0,'ELISA = Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay; used to detect antigens or antibodies.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Environmental Issues','easy','Depletion of the ozone layer is mainly caused by:','["CFCs","CO₂","SO₂","NOx"]',0,'Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) release Cl radicals that catalytically destroy ozone molecules.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Biodiversity','medium','The hotspot of biodiversity in India includes:','["Western Ghats","Rajasthan desert","Gangetic plains","Himalayan foothills only"]',0,'India has 4 biodiversity hotspots: Western Ghats, Eastern Himalayas, Indo-Burma, Sundaland.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Human Health','medium','The causative agent of malaria is:','["Plasmodium vivax","Leishmania","Wuchereria","Entamoeba histolytica"]',0,'Malaria is caused by Plasmodium species (P. vivax, P. falciparum, P. malariae, P. ovale).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Human Health','hard','Interferons are produced by virus-infected cells and act by:','["Inducing antiviral proteins in neighbouring cells","Killing viruses directly","Producing antibodies","Activating B cells"]',0,'Interferons are cytokines that signal neighbouring cells to produce antiviral proteins.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','hard','In incomplete dominance, the F2 ratio for flower colour (Red × White) is:','["1:2:1 (Red:Pink:White)","3:1","1:1","2:1:1"]',0,'Incomplete dominance: F1=all pink; F2=1 red:2 pink:1 white (1:2:1 genotypic and phenotypic ratio).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','medium','A food chain always starts with:','["Producers (green plants)","Decomposers","Primary consumers","Omnivores"]',0,'Food chains always begin with producers (autotrophs/green plants) that fix solar energy.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Animal Kingdom','medium','The respiratory pigment in cockroach is:','["Haemolymph (no respiratory pigment)","Haemoglobin","Haemocyanin","Myoglobin"]',0,'Cockroaches have open circulatory system with haemolymph; O₂ is carried by tracheal system directly — no respiratory pigment.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Structural Organisation','medium','Which type of epithelium lines the inner surface of blood vessels?','["Simple squamous","Stratified squamous","Columnar","Cuboidal"]',0,'The inner lining of blood vessels (endothelium) is simple squamous epithelium.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Structural Organisation','hard','Haversian canals are found in:','["Compact bone","Spongy bone","Cartilage","Tendon"]',0,'Haversian canals run longitudinally through compact bone, containing blood vessels and nerves.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Molecular Biology','hard','Which of the following is NOT a post-transcriptional modification in eukaryotes?','["5-capping","Polyadenylation","Splicing of introns","Methylation of bases in rRNA"]',3,'Methylation of rRNA bases is a ribosomal modification; 5-cap, poly-A tail, and splicing are post-transcriptional mRNA modifications.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Biotechnology','medium','The Ti plasmid used in plant genetic engineering comes from:','["Agrobacterium tumefaciens","E. coli","Bacillus thuringiensis","Rhizobium"]',0,'Ti plasmid (tumour-inducing) is found in Agrobacterium tumefaciens and used to introduce genes into plants.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Reproduction','medium','Sertoli cells provide nourishment to:','["Developing sperms","Eggs","Oogonia","Corpus luteum"]',0,'Sertoli (nurse) cells in seminiferous tubules nourish and support developing sperm cells.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','medium','Peristalsis is the movement of:','["Alimentary canal","Heart muscle","Skeletal muscle","Only oesophagus"]',0,'Peristalsis — wave-like muscular contractions — moves food through the alimentary (digestive) canal.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Physiology','medium','Water potential (Ψ) of pure water is:','["Zero","Positive","Negative","−0.23 MPa"]',0,'Water potential of pure water at standard conditions is zero (reference state).','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Photosynthesis','medium','Which gas is released during the light-dependent reaction of photosynthesis?','["O₂","CO₂","N₂","H₂"]',0,'O₂ is released by photolysis of water during the light reactions at PS II.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','medium','The functional unit of kidney is:','["Nephron","Glomerulus","Bowman capsule","Loop of Henle"]',0,'The nephron is the structural and functional unit of the kidney.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','medium','Dihybrid cross ratio in F2 generation (two independently assorting traits):','["9:3:3:1","1:2:1","3:1","1:1:1:1"]',0,'Dihybrid F2 phenotypic ratio is 9:3:3:1 (Mendel`s law of independent assortment).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','hard','Which type of species interaction benefits one species while harming another?','["Predation and parasitism","Mutualism","Commensalism","Amensalism"]',0,'Predation and parasitism are interactions where one species (predator/parasite) benefits at the expense of another.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Evolution','medium','Industrial melanism in Biston betularia moths is an example of:','["Natural selection","Genetic drift","Gene flow","Mutation pressure"]',0,'Peppered moth (Biston betularia) change — dark moths survived in polluted areas — demonstrates natural selection.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Molecular Biology','medium','Which of the following is correct about tRNA?','["It carries amino acids to the ribosome","It forms the ribosome","It is mRNA template","It synthesizes DNA"]',0,'tRNA (transfer RNA) carries specific amino acids to the ribosome during translation.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Biotechnology','hard','Bt toxin in Bt cotton is effective against:','["Insects (bollworm)","Fungi","Bacteria","Nematodes"]',0,'Bt toxin from Bacillus thuringiensis is a protoxin activated in insect midgut; effective against bollworm larvae (insects).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Animal Kingdom','hard','Flame cells are excretory organs in:','["Platyhelminthes","Annelida","Arthropoda","Mollusca"]',0,'Flame cells (protonephridia) are the excretory units in platyhelminthes (flatworms).','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Human Health','medium','AIDS is caused by:','["HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus)","HBV","HPV","HSV"]',0,'AIDS is caused by HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) which attacks CD4+ T helper cells.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Environmental Issues','medium','BOD (Biochemical Oxygen Demand) is a measure of:','["Organic pollution in water","Air pollution","Soil fertility","Noise pollution"]',0,'BOD measures the amount of oxygen consumed by microorganisms to decompose organic matter in water — indicates organic pollution.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Plant Kingdom','medium','Heterospory (two types of spores) evolved for the first time in:','["Pteridophytes","Bryophytes","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms"]',0,'Heterospory (megaspores and microspores) first appeared in some pteridophytes — a precursor to seed habit.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Biology','Genetics','easy','The sex of an individual in humans is determined by:','["Chromosome from father","Chromosome from mother","Both parents","Environment"]',0,'The Y chromosome (from father) determines male sex; XX = female (from father`s X); sex determined by paternal chromosome.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Biology','Human Physiology','hard','Which digestive enzyme is secreted in inactive form (zymogen)?','["Pepsinogen","Salivary amylase","Lipase","Sucrase"]',0,'Pepsinogen (inactive) is converted to pepsin (active) by HCl in the stomach.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Biology','Ecology','medium','Which gas is primarily responsible for acid rain?','["SO₂ and NOx","CO₂","CO","CH₄"]',0,'Acid rain is primarily caused by SO₂ and NOx emissions that form H₂SO₄ and HNO₃ in the atmosphere.','NCERT Class 12',2024),

-- ====== NEET — PHYSICS (79 questions) ======
('NEET','Physics','Motion','easy','A body moves with uniform velocity. Net force on it is:','["Zero","Equal to its weight","In direction of motion","Opposite to motion"]',0,'Newton`s 1st law: uniform velocity means zero acceleration → zero net force.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Motion','medium','A body travels first half of distance with speed v₁ and second half with v₂. Average speed is:','["2v₁v₂/(v₁+v₂)","(v₁+v₂)/2","√(v₁v₂)","v₁v₂/(v₁+v₂)"]',0,'Average speed = total distance/total time = 2d/[d/v₁+d/v₂] = 2v₁v₂/(v₁+v₂).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Laws of Motion','easy','Action and reaction forces act on:','["Different objects","Same object","Same object in same direction","Perpendicular to each other"]',0,'Newton`s 3rd law: action-reaction forces are equal, opposite, and act on different bodies.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Laws of Motion','medium','A 1000 kg car accelerates from 0 to 20 m/s in 10 s. Force applied (ignoring friction):','["2000 N","1000 N","200 N","20000 N"]',0,'F=ma=1000×2=2000 N; a=(20-0)/10=2 m/s².','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Work and Energy','medium','A ball is thrown up with kinetic energy 100 J. At maximum height, potential energy is:','["100 J","0 J","50 J","200 J"]',0,'At maximum height, all KE converts to PE (ignoring air resistance) → PE = 100 J.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Gravitation','easy','The gravitational force between two masses is:','["Inversely proportional to square of distance","Proportional to square of distance","Inversely proportional to distance","Proportional to distance"]',0,'Newton`s law: F = Gm₁m₂/r² — inversely proportional to r².','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Gravitation','medium','Value of g at centre of Earth is:','["Zero","9.8 m/s²","Infinite","Half of surface value"]',0,'At the centre of Earth, g=0 (gravitational pull is equal from all directions, net=0).','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Properties of Matter','medium','Surface tension of a liquid causes:','["Minimum surface area","Maximum surface area","No surface effect","Increased volume"]',0,'Surface tension causes liquid surfaces to contract to minimum area (e.g., water drops form spheres).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Thermodynamics','easy','In an isochoric process, work done is:','["Zero","Maximum","Negative","Positive"]',0,'Isochoric = constant volume → ΔV=0 → W=PΔV=0.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Thermodynamics','medium','First law of thermodynamics states:','["Energy is conserved","Entropy increases","Heat flows from hot to cold","Absolute zero cannot be reached"]',0,'First law: ΔU=Q−W; energy is conserved in thermodynamic processes.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Oscillations','medium','Time period of a simple pendulum of length L on Earth (g):','["2π√(L/g)","2π√(g/L)","π√(L/g)","2πL/g"]',0,'T=2π√(L/g) for simple pendulum (small oscillations).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Waves','easy','Which wave cannot travel through vacuum?','["Sound","Light","X-rays","Radio waves"]',0,'Sound waves are mechanical longitudinal waves requiring a material medium; cannot travel in vacuum.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Electrostatics','easy','SI unit of electric charge is:','["Coulomb","Ampere","Volt","Farad"]',0,'SI unit of charge is Coulomb (C); 1 C = 1 A·s.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Electrostatics','medium','A point charge q is at the centre of a cube. Total electric flux through the cube (ε₀):','["q/ε₀","q/(6ε₀)","6q/ε₀","q/(8ε₀)"]',0,'Gauss law: total flux = q_enclosed/ε₀ = q/ε₀ (irrespective of shape).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Current Electricity','easy','Ohm`s law states that (at constant temperature):','["V ∝ I","V ∝ 1/I","V ∝ I²","I ∝ V²"]',0,'Ohm`s law: V = IR → V ∝ I at constant resistance (temperature).','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Current Electricity','medium','Power dissipated in resistor R carrying current I is:','["I²R","IR","I²/R","IR²"]',0,'P=I²R (or P=V²/R or P=VI); power in a resistor = I²R.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Magnetism','easy','A magnetic field exerts force on:','["Moving charges","Stationary charges","Both moving and stationary","Neither"]',0,'Magnetic force F=qv×B acts only on moving charges (v≠0).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Magnetism','medium','A current-carrying straight wire is placed in a magnetic field. Force on it is zero when:','["Wire is parallel to field","Wire is perpendicular to field","Wire is at 45°","Always zero"]',0,'F=BIL sinθ; when θ=0° (wire parallel to field), sinθ=0 → F=0.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Electromagnetic Induction','medium','Lenz`s law is a consequence of:','["Conservation of energy","Conservation of momentum","Newton`s 3rd law","Ampere`s law"]',0,'Lenz`s law states induced current opposes cause — this is a consequence of conservation of energy.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Optics','easy','The speed of light in vacuum is approximately:','["3×10⁸ m/s","3×10⁶ m/s","3×10¹⁰ m/s","3×10⁴ m/s"]',0,'Speed of light c = 3×10⁸ m/s (299,792,458 m/s exactly).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Optics','medium','Total internal reflection occurs when light goes from:','["Denser to rarer medium at angle > critical angle","Rarer to denser at any angle","Denser to rarer at any angle","Rarer to denser at angle > critical angle"]',0,'TIR occurs when light travels from denser to rarer medium and angle of incidence exceeds critical angle.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Modern Physics','easy','Photoelectric work function is the:','["Minimum energy to eject an electron","Maximum energy of ejected electron","Energy of incident photon","Kinetic energy of photon"]',0,'Work function (φ) is the minimum energy required to eject an electron from the metal surface.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Modern Physics','medium','Alpha particle consists of:','["2 protons + 2 neutrons","1 proton + 1 neutron","2 protons + 1 neutron","Electron + proton"]',0,'Alpha particle (⁴He nucleus) = 2 protons + 2 neutrons.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Modern Physics','hard','Threshold frequency for photoelectric effect depends on:','["Nature of metal","Intensity of light","Frequency of light","Both intensity and frequency"]',0,'Threshold frequency depends only on the nature (work function) of the metal surface.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Semiconductor','medium','Which of the following is a p-type semiconductor dopant?','["Boron","Phosphorus","Arsenic","Antimony"]',0,'Boron (group 13) has 3 valence electrons; as dopant in Si it creates holes → p-type semiconductor.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Motion','hard','A stone is thrown horizontally from height H. It lands at horizontal distance x from the base. Its initial velocity was:','["x√(g/2H)","x√(g/H)","x/(√(2H/g))","All equivalent to x√(g/2H)"]',3,'H=½gt² → t=√(2H/g); x=v₀t → v₀=x/t=x√(g/2H).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Optics','hard','In YDSE, if one slit is closed, the pattern on screen changes from:','["Interference to diffraction pattern","Diffraction to interference pattern","No change","Both disappear"]',0,'With both slits: interference fringes. With one slit closed: single-slit diffraction pattern.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Current Electricity','hard','In a potentiometer, the length of wire is 1 m and balance length for 1.5 V cell is 60 cm. Balance length for 2 V cell is:','["80 cm","75 cm","90 cm","60 cm"]',0,'l₁/l₂ = E₁/E₂ → 60/l₂=1.5/2 → l₂=80 cm.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Electrostatics','hard','Two identical metal spheres (charge +3q and −q) are brought in contact and separated. Charge on each:','["+q","+2q","0","+3q"]',0,'Total charge=3q+(−q)=2q; on contact they share equally → +q each.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Thermodynamics','hard','A gas expands adiabatically. Temperature of gas:','["Decreases","Increases","Remains same","Increases then decreases"]',0,'In adiabatic expansion, no heat exchange; work is done at the expense of internal energy → temperature decreases.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Waves','medium','The frequency of sound as heard by observer moving towards stationary source (Doppler effect) is:','["Higher than actual","Lower than actual","Same as actual","Zero"]',0,'Observer moving towards source → apparent frequency increases (Doppler effect).','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Properties of Matter','hard','A wire of length L, area A, Young`s modulus Y is stretched by force F. Extension is:','["FL/(AY)","FAY/L","FL/(Y)","F/(AYL)"]',0,'Y=stress/strain=FL/(AΔL) → ΔL=FL/(AY).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Electromagnetic Induction','hard','A rod of length L moves with velocity v perpendicular to field B. EMF induced is:','["BLv","BL²v","BLv²","BL/v"]',0,'Motional EMF ε=BLv (rod moving perpendicular to both its length and B field).','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Gravitation','hard','Two planets of mass M and 4M, radii R and 2R. Escape velocity from planet 2 compared to planet 1:','["√2 times","2 times","Equal","4 times"]',0,'v_e=√(2GM/R); v_e2/v_e1=√(4M/M × R/2R)=√(2)=√2.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Magnetism','hard','Magnetic susceptibility of diamagnetic materials is:','["Small and negative","Large and positive","Zero","Small and positive"]',0,'Diamagnetic materials have small negative magnetic susceptibility (repelled weakly by magnetic fields).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Optics','medium','Power of a lens with focal length −25 cm is:','["−4 D","4 D","−0.25 D","25 D"]',0,'P=1/f(m)=1/(−0.25)=−4 D.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Motion','medium','Velocity-time graph of uniform acceleration is a:','["Straight line with positive slope","Horizontal line","Parabola","Curve"]',0,'For uniform acceleration, v=u+at → v vs t is a straight line with slope a.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Work and Energy','hard','A spring of spring constant k is compressed by x. If mass m is placed on it and released, height it rises to:','["kx²/(2mg)","kx/mg","k²x/(2mg)","kx²/mg"]',0,'½kx²=mgh → h=kx²/(2mg).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Modern Physics','medium','In Bohr`s model, radius of nth orbit is proportional to:','["n²","n","1/n²","n³"]',0,'Bohr radius r_n=a₀n²/Z; for hydrogen (Z=1), r_n ∝ n².','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Semiconductor','hard','In a full-wave rectifier, output frequency is:','["Double the input","Same as input","Half the input","Four times input"]',0,'Full-wave rectifier: both half-cycles are rectified → output frequency = 2 × input frequency.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Electrostatics','medium','Dielectric constant (K) of vacuum is:','["1","0","Infinity","8.85×10⁻¹²"]',0,'Dielectric constant (relative permittivity) of vacuum is defined as 1 (reference value).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Oscillations','hard','Resonance occurs in a forced oscillator when:','["Driving frequency equals natural frequency","Amplitude is zero","Damping is maximum","Frequency is zero"]',0,'Resonance: driving frequency = natural frequency → maximum amplitude of oscillation.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Laws of Motion','hard','A rocket ejects mass dm/dt at exhaust velocity v_e. Thrust force is:','["v_e × dm/dt","v_e² × dm/dt","v_e × (dm/dt)²","v_e/(dm/dt)"]',0,'Rocket thrust = v_e × (−dm/dt); reaction force to expelled exhaust.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Physics','Current Electricity','medium','The resistance of a conductor at temperature T (R₀ at 0°C, α=temperature coefficient):','["R₀(1+αT)","R₀(1−αT)","R₀αT","R₀/T"]',0,'R_T=R₀(1+αT) for most conductors (positive temperature coefficient of resistance).','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Physics','Optics','medium','A ray of light enters a glass slab at 30° to the normal. If n=1.5, angle of refraction is:','["sin⁻¹(1/3) ≈ 19.5°","30°","45°","60°"]',0,'n sinr=sin30°=0.5 → sinr=0.5/1.5=1/3 → r≈19.5°.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Physics','Modern Physics','hard','Activity of a radioactive source (decay constant λ, N atoms) is:','["λN","λ/N","N/λ","λN²"]',0,'Activity A=λN (disintegrations per second); unit Becquerel (Bq).','NCERT Class 12',2023),

-- ====== NEET — CHEMISTRY (79 questions) ======
('NEET','Chemistry','Basic Concepts','easy','Avogadro number is approximately:','["6.022×10²³","6.022×10²²","6.022×10²⁴","1.6×10⁻¹⁹"]',0,'Avogadro number N_A = 6.022×10²³ mol⁻¹.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Atomic Structure','easy','The number of neutrons in ³⁷₁₇Cl (mass number 37, atomic number 17) is:','["20","17","37","3"]',0,'Neutrons = Mass number − Atomic number = 37−17 = 20.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Atomic Structure','medium','Which electronic configuration represents the ground state of Fe (Z=26)?','["[Ar] 3d⁶4s²","[Ar] 3d⁸","[Ar] 3d⁵4s¹","[Ar] 4s²3d⁶"]',0,'Fe: [Ar]3d⁶4s² — 3d filled before 4s in writing but 4s has lower energy for filling.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Chemical Bonding','easy','Hybridization of carbon in CH₄:','["sp³","sp²","sp","sp³d"]',0,'CH₄: 4 bond pairs, no lone pairs → tetrahedral → sp³ hybridization.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Chemical Bonding','medium','VSEPR theory predicts the shape of H₂O as:','["Bent (V-shaped)","Linear","Tetrahedral","Trigonal planar"]',0,'H₂O: 2 bond pairs + 2 lone pairs → bent/V-shaped geometry.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','States of Matter','easy','At STP (0°C, 1 atm), volume of 1 mol ideal gas is:','["22.4 L","22.7 L","11.2 L","44.8 L"]',0,'Molar volume of ideal gas at STP = 22.4 L/mol.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','States of Matter','medium','Graham`s law of diffusion: rate of diffusion is inversely proportional to:','["Square root of molar mass","Molar mass","Square of molar mass","Density directly"]',0,'r ∝ 1/√M — Graham`s law; lighter gases diffuse faster.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Thermodynamics','easy','Enthalpy change (ΔH) at constant pressure equals:','["Heat exchanged (q_p)","Work done","Internal energy change","Free energy"]',0,'ΔH = q_p (heat exchanged at constant pressure).','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Thermodynamics','medium','Standard enthalpy of combustion of CH₄ is −890 kJ/mol. Heat released by burning 4 g CH₄ (M=16):','["222.5 kJ","890 kJ","3560 kJ","445 kJ"]',0,'4 g = 0.25 mol; heat = 0.25×890 = 222.5 kJ.','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Equilibrium','easy','pH of a neutral solution at 25°C is:','["7","0","14","10"]',0,'At 25°C, neutral solution has [H⁺]=[OH⁻]=10⁻⁷ M → pH=7.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Equilibrium','medium','Ka of weak acid HA = 10⁻⁵. pH of 0.1 M solution:','["3","5","6","4"]',0,'[H⁺]=√(Ka×C)=√(10⁻⁵×0.1)=√(10⁻⁶)=10⁻³ → pH=3.','NCERT Class 11',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Redox','easy','When a substance is oxidised, it:','["Loses electrons","Gains electrons","Loses protons","Gains protons"]',0,'Oxidation = loss of electrons (OIL RIG mnemonic).','NCERT Class 11',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Organic Chemistry','easy','The functional group −COOH is present in:','["Carboxylic acids","Alcohols","Aldehydes","Esters"]',0,'−COOH (carboxyl group) is the characteristic functional group of carboxylic acids.','NCERT Class 11',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Organic Chemistry','medium','Which compound shows optical isomerism?','["Lactic acid (CH₃CHOHCOOH)","Methane","Ethene","Benzene"]',0,'Lactic acid has a chiral carbon (4 different groups) → optical isomerism.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Electrochemistry','medium','In electrolysis of water, which gas is produced at cathode?','["Hydrogen","Oxygen","Chlorine","Both hydrogen and oxygen"]',0,'At cathode (reduction): 2H⁺+2e⁻ → H₂; at anode: 4OH⁻ → 2H₂O+O₂+4e⁻.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Chemical Kinetics','easy','Catalyst increases rate of reaction by:','["Lowering activation energy","Increasing activation energy","Increasing temperature","Changing equilibrium"]',0,'Catalyst provides an alternative pathway with lower activation energy, increasing reaction rate.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Surface Chemistry','medium','Adsorption is:','["Accumulation of substance on surface","Absorption into bulk","Reaction with surface","None"]',0,'Adsorption: accumulation of substance (adsorbate) on the surface of adsorbent.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','p-Block Elements','easy','Hybridization of sulphur in SF₆:','["sp³d²","sp³","sp²","sp³d"]',0,'SF₆: 6 bond pairs → octahedral → sp³d² hybridization.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Coordination Chemistry','medium','The coordination number of Co in [Co(NH₃)₆]³⁺ is:','["6","3","4","12"]',0,'Coordination number = number of ligands bonded to central atom = 6 (six NH₃ ligands).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Biomolecules','easy','The monomer of proteins is:','["Amino acid","Glucose","Nucleotide","Fatty acid"]',0,'Proteins are polymers of amino acids linked by peptide bonds.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Polymers','medium','Nylon 6,6 is formed from:','["Hexamethylenediamine + adipic acid","Caprolactam","Glucose","Amino acids"]',0,'Nylon 6,6 is a condensation polymer of hexamethylene diamine and adipic acid.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Haloalkanes','medium','The reaction of alkyl halide with KOH (aqueous) gives:','["Alcohol","Alkene","Alkyne","Ether"]',0,'Alkyl halide + KOH (aqueous) → substitution → alcohol (SN2 or SN1).','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Aldehydes Ketones','medium','Aldol condensation occurs in compounds having:','["α-hydrogen (adjacent to C=O)","No hydrogen","Only aromatic compounds","Compounds with OH group"]',0,'Aldol condensation requires α-hydrogen adjacent to the carbonyl group.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Amines','easy','Primary amines react with HNO₂ to give:','["Diazonium salt","Secondary amine","Amide","Alcohol"]',0,'Primary amines + HNO₂ → diazonium salts (important in synthesis, e.g., azo dyes).','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Solid State','easy','NaCl has which type of crystal structure?','["Face-centred cubic (FCC)","Body-centred cubic (BCC)","Simple cubic","Hexagonal"]',0,'NaCl has FCC/rock salt structure: Na⁺ in octahedral voids of Cl⁻ FCC arrangement.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','Solutions','easy','Molality is defined as moles of solute per:','["Kilogram of solvent","Litre of solution","100 g of solution","Mole of solution"]',0,'Molality (m) = moles of solute / kg of solvent.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Solutions','medium','Henry`s law: amount of gas dissolved in liquid at constant temperature is proportional to:','["Partial pressure of gas","Temperature","Volume of liquid","Molar mass of gas"]',0,'Henry`s law: p = K_H × x; amount dissolved ∝ partial pressure of the gas.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','d-Block Elements','medium','Which transition metal is used as a catalyst in Haber process for NH₃ synthesis?','["Iron","Nickel","Platinum","Copper"]',0,'Iron (with Al₂O₃/K₂O promoters) is the catalyst in Haber process: N₂+3H₂→2NH₃.','NCERT Class 12',2023),
('NEET','Chemistry','p-Block Elements','medium','Bleaching powder is:','["Ca(OCl)Cl","CaCl₂","Ca(OH)₂","CaO"]',0,'Bleaching powder = Ca(OCl)Cl (calcium hypochlorite chloride); active ingredient is hypochlorite.','NCERT Class 12',2022),
('NEET','Chemistry','Organic Chemistry','hard','Which reagent converts primary alcohol to aldehyde without over-oxidation?','["PCC (pyridinium chlorochromate)","KMnO₄","K₂Cr₂O₇/H₂SO₄","CrO₃"]',0,'PCC (mild oxidant) converts 1° alcohol to aldehyde without further oxidation to carboxylic acid.','NCERT Class 12',2024),
('NEET','Chemistry','Atomic Structure','hard','If n=4, possible values of azimuthal quantum number l are:','["0,1,2,3","0,1,2","1,2,3,4","0,1"]',0,'l ranges from 0 to n−1; for n=4: l=0,1,2,3 (s,p,d,f subshells).','NCERT Class 11',2023),
